S("Name five careers in science and state one thing each person does",5,"Medical doctor diagnoses illness; pharmacist prepares medicines; engineer designs and builds structures and power systems; meteorologist forecasts weather; science teacher teaches science.",CAR),
S("Name three careers in science",3,"Medical doctor, pharmacist, engineer, veterinarian, meteorologist, food scientist, teacher and others.","One science career::doctor,nurse,pharmacist,laboratory,agricultural,veterinarian,food scientist,engineer,environmental,geologist,meteorologist,computer,software,teacher,astronomer,physicist|A second career::doctor,nurse,pharmacist,laboratory,agricultural,veterinarian,food scientist,engineer,environmental,geologist,meteorologist,computer,software,teacher,astronomer,physicist|A third career::doctor,nurse,pharmacist,laboratory,agricultural,veterinarian,food scientist,engineer,environmental,geologist,meteorologist,computer,software,teacher,astronomer,physicist"),
S("Explain how a meteorologist helps farmers",2,"A meteorologist studies and forecasts the weather and warns farmers and communities about rain, floods and storms, so farmers can plan planting and protect their crops.","Studies and forecasts the weather::weather,forecast,forecasts|Warns farmers about rain, floods and storms::warns,warn,rain,floods,storms"),
S("State two ways in which science and technology are used in the home",2,"Refrigerators keep food from spoiling, cookers and LED lamps use energy efficiently, and mobile phones connect families.","Refrigerators keep food from spoiling::refrigerator,fridge,spoil,food|Cookers, LED lamps or mobile phones::cooker,led,lamps,phones,mobile,phone"),
S("Choose one career and explain why Ghana needs more people in it",2,"For example agriculture and food processing: most Ghanaians depend on farming and processing adds value and reduces waste. Any career with a reason from the chapter is acceptable.",FOCUS),
S("Name two science careers that you think Ghana should focus on",4,"Agriculture and food processing (most Ghanaians farm); health sciences (a healthy population can learn and work); renewable energy and engineering; ICT; environmental science; science and maths teaching.",FOCUS),
S("Why does Ghana need many science teachers",2,"Every other career depends on good teachers, and science teachers prepare the next generation of scientists.","Every other career depends on good teachers::every,depends,careers,good teachers|They prepare the next generation of scientists::next generation,prepare,scientists"),
S("State two achievements of Professor Francis Allotey",2,"He was the first Ghanaian full professor of mathematics, is known for the Allotey formalism, led the Ghana Academy of Arts and Sciences and helped found the African Physical Society.",
  "First Ghanaian full professor of mathematics::first,professor,mathematics|Allotey formalism from soft X ray spectroscopy::formalism,x ray,spectroscopy|Led the Ghana Academy of Arts and Sciences::academy|Helped found the African Physical Society::african physical society,physical society"),
S("Name the scientist who discovered penicillin",2,"Alexander Fleming discovered penicillin in 1928; it was the first widely used antibiotic and treats bacterial infections.",PEN),
S("State the importance of the discovery of penicillin",2,"Penicillin was the first widely used antibiotic, so it made it possible to treat bacterial infections.",PEN),
S("Choose one scientist and say what career is linked to the work",1,"For example Alexander Fleming: microbiologist and doctor; Albert Einstein: physicist; Charles Darwin: naturalist and biologist; Stephen Hawking: physicist and cosmologist.","A scientist with the linked career (physicist, microbiologist, biologist, cosmologist, biochemist, food scientist)::physicist,microbiologist,doctor,biologist,naturalist,cosmologist,biochemist,mathematician,food scientist,teacher,educator"),
S("Explain why a portfolio helps you to learn about the impact of science",2,"It makes you research a theme, collect information and pictures from different sources, arrange it under headings and present it, so you learn how science has changed homes, schools, communities and the universe.",
  "You research and collect information and pictures from different sources::research,collect,information,sources|You arrange and present it, learning how science has changed life::arrange,present,presentation,changed,impact,homes,communities"),
S("State what a pharmacist does",2,"A pharmacist prepares and gives medicines and advises on their use, making sure they are safe and correct.","Prepares and gives medicines::prepares,gives,medicines,medicine|Advises on their use and makes sure they are safe::advises,advice,safe,correct"),
S("Explain how an engineer improves life in a community",2,"An engineer designs and builds structures, machines and power systems, providing roads, buildings, electricity and water.","Designs and builds structures, machines and power systems::designs,builds,structures,machines,power|Providing roads, buildings, electricity or water::roads,buildings,electricity,water"),
S("State one achievement of Professor Ewurama Addy",1,"She showed the value of the herb Desmodium adscendens in treating asthma, was the first Ghanaian woman full professor of natural science, first quiz mistress of the National Science and Maths Quiz, and won the 1999 UNESCO Kalinga Prize.","An achievement such as herbal medicine research, first woman full professor, first quiz mistress or the Kalinga Prize::herbal,herb,asthma,desmodium,first,quiz,kalinga,professor"),
S("State one area of research of Professor Ibok Oduro",1,"Indigenous and underused African crops such as sweet potato, yam bean and breadfruit, and turning them into foods and other products.","Indigenous or underused African crops (sweet potato, yam bean, breadfruit) and food products::crops,sweet potato,yam bean,breadfruit,indigenous,underused,food"),
S("State one achievement of Albert Einstein",1,"He developed the theory of relativity and explained the photoelectric effect, winning the 1921 Nobel Prize in Physics.","Theory of relativity or photoelectric effect (Nobel Prize 1921)::relativity,photoelectric,nobel"),
S("Name one place where science and technology are used in a school",1,"Computers, projectors and science laboratories help learners study, and filters make drinking water safe.","A school example such as a laboratory, computers, projectors or water filters::laboratory,laboratories,computers,projector,projectors,filters,filter"),
S("A community has frequent outbreaks of diarrhoea",3,"A medical laboratory scientist tests samples to find the cause; a doctor or nurse diagnoses and treats patients; an environmental scientist studies pollution and waste; an engineer provides water and sanitation systems.",
  "Medical laboratory scientist tests samples to find the cause::laboratory,tests,samples,cause|Doctor or nurse diagnoses and treats patients::doctor,nurse,diagnose,treat|Environmental scientist or engineer helps with pollution, waste or safe water::environmental,engineer,water,waste,pollution,sanitation"),
S("A farmer loses a large part of the tomato harvest",2,"A food scientist, who studies how to process, preserve and improve food, could help by preserving the tomatoes (for example making tomato paste) so less is wasted.","A food scientist (or agricultural scientist)::food scientist,agricultural|Who studies how to process and preserve food, reducing waste::process,preserve,preserving,waste"),
S("A town is hit by floods every rainy season",3,"The meteorologist forecasts rain and warns the community; the environmental scientist studies waste, blocked drains and climate; the engineer designs and builds drains, bridges and structures.",
  "Meteorologist forecasts weather and warns of rain and floods::meteorologist,forecast,warn,rain,floods|Environmental scientist studies pollution, waste and climate::environmental,waste,pollution,climate|Engineer designs and builds structures such as drains::engineer,designs,builds,drains,structures"),
S("Choose one scientist from this chapter and explain how the person's work could inspire",2,"For example Alexander Fleming discovered penicillin, showing that careful observation can save millions of lives. Any scientist's achievement from the chapter, with a link to the young learner's life, is acceptable.",
  "A scientist's achievement from the chapter::allotey,addy,oduro,einstein,fleming,darwin,hawking,penicillin,relativity,evolution|How it can inspire a learner (asking questions, working hard, not giving up)::inspire,questions,work hard,hard,give up,solve,community"),
